<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yadavindra Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1913–1974</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yadavindra Singh was the last ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of Patiala, reigning from 1938, and served as Chancellor of the Chamber of Princes. He acceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in 1947 and in 1948 became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajpramukh">Rajpramukh</a>, the constitutional head, of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patiala-and-east-punjab-states-union">Patiala and East Punjab States Union</a>, which was merged into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> in 1956. He later served as an Indian ambassador and was a noted cricketer.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yadavindra-singh.jpg" alt="Yadavindra Singh" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rob Mieremet for Anefo · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yadvinder_Singh_Mahendra_Bahadur_(1971).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
